nazuchem-s2n source provenance
=============================

This structure-to-name engine began as a port of openclatura 0.4.3, extended
in ReShiki, where it previously lived in src/naming/openclatura/. Source headers
and the repository-root PROVENANCE-nazuchem.toml preserve the original ancestry
and function-level boundaries; packaging it as a library does not make
incorporated algorithms original nazuchem code.

openclatura 0.4.3, commit 90dc5bcb4910c196122ec0405d06a32929a8f308:
https://github.com/lamalab-org/openclatura
Copyright (c) 2026 lamalab-org. Complete MIT terms and source/data attribution
are in licenses/openclatura/LICENSE and licenses/openclatura/NOTICE.

OPSIN by Daniel Lowe:
https://github.com/dan2097/opsin
Copyright 2017 Daniel Lowe. Incorporated nomenclature registries include
material from OPSIN 2.9.0, commit b91b610af5ab07560fedb20730d7aef46bb2bca0,
and data inherited through openclatura whose generating OPSIN revision was
not recorded. In particular, fusion_entry_geometry.json derives from OPSIN
2.9.0 FusedRingNumberer.java; it records parser compatibility, not IUPAC PIN
certification. Retained macrocycle and fused-hydrocarbon template generation
has no recorded OPSIN revision; the current n2s port pin is not asserted for
those data. Complete MIT terms and the existing broader port notice are in
licenses/opsin/LICENSE and licenses/opsin/NOTICE. The per-file ledger records
the incorporated sources and unresolved pins.

src/python_int_set.rs adapts CPython 3.12 Objects/setobject.c under
Python-2.0. Its exact patch release/commit is unresolved. The complete licence
and history are in licenses/cpython/LICENSE; licenses/cpython/NOTICE retains
the existing attribution and distinguishes this source from the independently
pinned numeric adaptations elsewhere in ReShiki. This safe Rust code does
not include or invoke the Python interpreter.

The copied upstream notices retain their original ReShiki path references
and broader inventories. References to src/naming/openclatura/ in them now
identify this crate's src/; they do not assert that every listed ReShiki
component is incorporated here. Root copies remain for ReShiki's retained
implementations and reference corpora.

Original ReShiki/nazuchem code uses MIT OR Apache-2.0; see LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE. Pending owner decision: src/data/bluebook/p25_retained.tsv
retains NOASSERTION for its unresolved IUPAC table reuse permission/licensing
and unpinned web revision. The manifest expression records established terms
only, not a grant for unresolved material; publish = false is retained.
PubChem-derived reference corpora retained outside this crate are test-only;
their unresolved source terms are not covered by the local dual-licence grant.
